ther that soon  overtakes it as the center of the story  Duke's death is merely one piece of a  much bigger puzzle as it turns out miles  wasn't the intended victim but was in  fact the killer everyone was too busy  watching birdie dance as miles has  instructed them to do to note that Miles  handed Duke his glass intentionally it  wasn't even poisoned in the drink that  killed duke it was pineapple juice to  which Duke's allergic no pineapple on  that right Duke don't dance with  pineapple Duke was a useful Pawn in  Miles attempt to get away with the other  murder he committed miles refuses to use  any communication technology Beyond fax  machines but Duke is constantly getting  news notifications on his phone it's  through Duke's constant Google Alerts  that Miles finds out that Angie's death  has been reported in the news to prevent  anyone else finding out about that news  miles kills Duke taking both his phone  and his gun  while everyone is panicking about Duke's  death all the lights in the Mansion  suddenly go out miles claims this is  something that was planned as part of  the original murder mystery game a bit  of really unfortunate timing of course  that's not true miles has in fact stolen  the idea of putting a loaded gun on the  table and turning off the lights from  Benoit as Andy and Benoit regroup  outside miles shoots her through a  nearby window when everyone else arrives  at the scene it looks as if Andy is  bleeding to death but Andy isn't  actually dead her journal was in her  chest pocket and blocked the bullet she  and Benoit quickly concoct a plan to  fake her death using some of Jeremy  renner's hot sauce as fake blood we also  soon learned that Andy isn't really Andy  either the real Andy is dead this is her  twin sister Helen one of the many twists  in Glass Onion is that Janelle Monae  actually plays two characters there's  Andy the businesswoman whose company was  stolen by Miles and then there's her  identical twin sister Helen a  schoolteacher who's been on the Island  posing as Andy the whole time the real  Andy was responsible for introducing  miles to his future friends at their  local bar the Glass Onion it was on one  of that Bar's napkins that she sketched  out the plan for the tech Empire that  would make miles famous miles wasn't  particularly intelligent himself but he  was rich and could pay smarter more  talented people to do his work for him  eventually miles self-mythologizing led  him to cut Andy out of his business  after she tells him clear is too  dangerous to use as an energy source he  wrote his own version of the napkin in  his own handwriting and Heather mutual  friends lie in court to give him all the  credit before she died Andy sent out an  email with a picture of herself holding  a red envelope threatening to use its  contents to destroy miles career miles  doesn't use email but Lionel faxed him  Andy's message with that information  miles paid Andy a surprise personal  visit nearly crashing his car into  Duke's motorcycle as he left he almost  got in an accident on his motorcycle he  was driving so fast Andy I almost got  pancaked miles poisoned Andy's drink and  stole the envelope  after finding Andy's invitation to the  party Helen hires Benoit to investigate  Andy's suspicious death Helen reasonably  suspected Foul Play Benoit has enough  Connections in the media to keep the  news of Andy's death temporarily under  wraps so nobody at the party except for  Helen Benoit and Andy's killer would  know that she was dead to find out who  that killer was Benoit suggests that  Helen impersonate her sister on miles's  island the Revelation that Helen has  been posing as Andy re-contextualizes  all her interactions with everyone on  the island and we see flashbacks to what  she's really been up to she listens in  on the other partygoers conversations to  try to identify both specific motives  and potential opportunities for them to  have committed Andy's murder much to  benoit'