ven come close to the  island miles Burns Angie's original  napkin effectively destroying the  chances of this case holding up in court  miles once again tries to control the  narrative through lies and his friends  still aren't brave enough to truly stand  up to him once that evidence is gone  there's nothing Benoit can do  except maybe  offer you some courage that courage  comes in the form of another drink and a  sample of clear to remind her just what  her sister was trying to stop  with the authorities unable to help  Helen takes matters into her own hands  the Glass Onion is filled with tacky  glass sculptures and Furniture so it's  an easy Act of protest for Helen to just  start wrecking the place after Benoit  takes his leave the other guests feeling  guilty about betraying Andy and lying on  Miles behalf eventually join in on the  destruction Helen caps off her Symphony  of Destruction by definitively  disproving miles's claims that clear is  safe Andy and secretly clearing Lionel  new putting the untested hydrogen-based  power source on the market would lead to  new equivalents of the Hindenburg  explosion Helen puts the theory into  practice by destroying the bar cart  lighting it on fire and then throwing  the sample clear crystal Benoit handed  her into the Flames this of course sets  off an explosion that destroys the Glass  Onion all the people inside miraculously  avoid injury and manage to escape but  miles's plans for Clear are cooked  miles's most ostentatious Showcase of  wealth was displaying the original Mona  Lisa inside a sound activated security  chamber he loaded out from the Louvre  while the museum was closed due to the  covid-19 pandemic 10 years earlier when  Andy first introduced miles to the rest  of her friends miles announced his goal  was to make something that would be  talked about in the same breath as the  Mona Lisa a pretentious turn of phrase  that confuses almost everyone who hears  it and what does that mean it basically  means he wants some form of an immortal  Legacy now thanks to Helen his wish is  granted but not for the reasons he was  hoping for when Helen makes the Glass  Onion go Hindenburg all she has to do is  hit the override button on the gloss  case protecting the Mona Lisa for the  Masterpiece to burn to a crisp this  grants miles His Wish in a truly ironic  sense his fuel will be mentioned  alongside the Mona Lisa as the cause of  its destruction it also shows that  nothing is really Immortal everything is  in permanent miles was obsessed with  Legacy and now his legacy is sure to be  a complete disaster even if he isn't  punished for the murders he's committed  sonian is filled with chekhov's guns  details introduced early on in the movie  that pay off later Benoit blanc's wild  genius is that he notices everything  around him and is able to place all  those things as part of a broader  narrative but as much as Glass Onion is  a satisfying example of its genre it's  also a comedy poking light fun in it one  example of how it does so is by  introducing a character with absolutely  no relevance to the mystery whatsoever  Daryl played by Noel segan who also  played Trooper Wagner in the first  knives out and has made appearances in  all of Ryan Johnson's films Daryl is  both a red herring and comic relief he's  a stoner guest just hanging out at the  Glass Onion but he's not part of the  party and has no connection to the big  Mysteries whenever he crosses paths with  the party guests there's a comedic  awkwardness particularly when Helen  breaks into his room while searching for  the Red Envelope at the end of the movie  he and Benoit share a lighter while  sitting outside and watching the  fireworks of the Glass Onion exploding  [Music]

